        "original_id": "e01760fb-44ae-5adf-b18d-4c3fd901e531",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl\n- People: Mohamed Sanu\n- Teams: Rutgers Scarlet Knights, UCF, Atlanta Falcons\n- Organizations: National Football League, Big East\n- Places: Tropicana Field, St. Petersburg, Florida\n\nFacts:\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's was the second edition of the college football bowl game and was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\n- Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24 in the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl.\n- Mohamed Sanu was the MVP of the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl.\n- In the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, Mohamed Sanu caught 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown and rushed 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\n- The 2009 Rutgers Scarlet Knights football team finished the season 9–4, went 3–4 in Big East play, and won the St. Petersburg Bowl 45–24 over UCF.\n- Mohamed Sanu Sr., born August 22, 1989, is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
